/-!
# The Alexander subbase theorem

A space is quasi-compact if its topology is generated by a subbase such that every covering
of the whole space by subbasic opens has a finite subcover.

This is registered directly as Mathlib's `compactSpace_generateFrom`, with quasi-compactness
expressed by `CompactSpace`, without a separation assumption.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 08ZP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08ZP)
